1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Bc4 e6 7. Bb3 a6 8. O-O Na5 9. f4 b5 10. e5 $5 (10. f5 e5 11. Nde2 Nxb3 12. axb3 Bb7 13. Ng3 b4 14. Nd5 Nxd5 15. exd5 Qb6+ 16. Kh1 Qb5) (10. a3) 10... dxe5 11. fxe5 Bc5 12. Be3 Nxb3 13. axb3 Nd5 14. Qf3 O-O 15. Nxd5 exd5 16. Nc6 Bxe3+ 17. Qxe3 Qc7 18. Nd4 Be6 19. Rf3 ({The game continuation given in Informator is} 19. Rf4 Kh8 20. Raf1 Rg8 21. Rh4 b4 22. Rf3 ({What makes this version of the score less plausible is that White could now have finished the game off with} 22. Nxe6 fxe6 23. Rxh7+ Kxh7 24. Qh3+ Kg6 25. Qxe6+ Kh7 26. Rf3 {, etc JS}) 22... Qc5 23. Rfh3 {1-0}) 19... a5 20. Rg3 Kh8 21. Rf1 Rg8 22. Rf4 b4 23. Rh4 Qc5 24. Rgh3 {Sources: CHESS, January 1968, Vol.33/547-8, p141; Informator 5/409} 1-0

