1. e4 d6 2. d4 g6 3. Nf3 Bg7 4. Bc4 Nf6 {(To here, Basman records in descriptive notation but now switches to algebraic)} 5. Qe2 c6 6. O-O Nxe4 7. Bxf7+ Kxf7 8. Qxe4 Rf8 9. Qh4 Kg8 {('Kf8')} 10. Bg5 Bf6 11. Nbd2 Bf5 12. c3 Qd7 13. Rfe1 Na6 14. Ne4 Bxe4 15. Rxe4 Nc7 16. Rae1 Rae8 17. Qg3 Rf7 18. h4 Bg7 19. h5 gxh5 20. Qh4 h6 21. Bd2 Nd5 22. Qg3 Nf6 23. Re6 Ng4 24. Bxh6 Rf6 25. Rxf6 exf6 {('gf:')} 26. Bxg7 Kxg7 27. Kf1 Rxe1+ 28. Nxe1 Kf7 29. Qd3 {('Qe3' - Basman's handwriting becoming very ragged in the run up to the move 30 time control)} f5 30. Nf3 Kg7 {No result recorded - presumably went to adjudication where it would probably have been given a draw, though White is +1.60 or so according to Stockfish 17. Source: Basman scoresheet (https://michael-basman-legacy.github.io/scoresheets/1973/Wimbledon%20Club%20Games%201973.pdf)} 1/2-1/2

