1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bb5+ Bd7 4. Bxd7+ Qxd7 5. O-O Nc6 6. c3 Nf6 7. Re1 g6 8. d4 cxd4 9. cxd4 Bg7 10. Nc3 O-O 11. Bg5 Ne8 12. Qa4 Nc7 13. d5 Ne5 14. Qxd7 Nxd7 15. Bxe7 Rfe8 16. Bxd6 Rac8 17. Rac1 Bxc3 18. Rxc3 Nb5 19. Rxc8 Rxc8 20. Bf4 Rc2 21. e5 Kf8 22. e6 fxe6 23. dxe6 Nc5 24. Ne5 Nd4 25. Nd7+ Ke8 26. Nf6+ Ke7 27. Nd5+ Ke8 28. Nc7+ {What looks like the original script of this scoresheet recorded only the names of players, moves and result. Later Basman has added "East Anglian Semi-Final Rnd 5" and "5-1-73". This was an allusion to the fact that this tournament was a qualifier for a later East Anglian tournament in which Bob Wade would be taking part. But the date and round number don't tally. 5-1-73 was day one of the tournament and we already have the game from that day. The only missing scores are rounds 3 (6-1-73) and 5 (7-1-73). I'm assuming it was round 5 but it may have been round 3 - JS. Source: Basman scoresheet (https://michael-basman-legacy.github.io/scoresheets/1973/Norwich%20Open%205-1-73.pdf)} 1-0

