{There is no score available of Basman's 3rd round game, in which I suspect he lost to the eventual tournament winner, Mitko Minev. His probable state of disappointment is reflected in some poor score-keeping in this game. JS} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. exd5 exd5 5. Qe2+ Ne7 6. Nf3 Nbc6 7. Qd3 Bf5 8. Qd1 Qd7 9. Be3 O-O-O 10. Bb5 f6 11. O-O g5 12. a3 Bxc3 13. bxc3 a6 14. Bd3 Na5 15. Nd2 Rhe8 16. Rb1 Bxd3 17. cxd3 Nf5 18. Qe2 Re6 19. Rfe1 Rde8 20. Nf1 Nh4 21. c4 Nc6 22. Qb2 Nd8 23. Qa2 {(The score reads 'Rb2' here which is not possible. The move chosen may not have been played but helps to make sense of what happens later - JS)} Rb6 24. Rb3 Ree6 25. c5 Rxb3 26. Qxb3 h6 27. Qd1 f5 28. Bd2 f4 29. Qg4 Nc6 30. Bc3 Re7 31. Qxd7+ Kxd7 {(Here the score reads 32 Rae1 Re8 which doesn't make much sense. I've added moves which help get us to the likeliest endgame position - JS)} 32. Rxe7+ Nxe7 33. Nd2 Nhf5 {('Nf5')} 34. Nf3 Nc6 35. g4 fxg3 36. hxg3 g4 37. Ne5+ Nxe5 38. dxe5 d4 39. Bd2 Ke7 {(The score reads Ke7 here)} 40. Kg2 Ke6 41. Bf4 h5 {(The rest of the game hangs together well except that a pair of half-moves have gone missing at some point - on the score Bf4/h5 are the 43nd moves.)} 42. f3 c6 43. fxg4 hxg4 44. Kf2 Ne7 45. Ke1 Ng6 46. Kf2 Nxe5 47. Bxe5 Kxe5 48. Ke2 Kd5 49. Kd2 Kxc5 50. Kc2 b5 51. Kb3 a5 52. Kb2 a4 53. Kc2 b4 54. Kb2 bxa3+ 55. Kxa3 Kb5 56. Kb2 Kb4 57. Ka2 c5 58. Kb2 c4 59. dxc4 Kxc4 {no result recorded, presumably White resigned Source: Basman scoresheet (https://michael-basman-legacy.github.io/scoresheets/1973/East%20Anglian%20Final%2011-5-73.pdf)} 0-1

