1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nf3 d6 4. Bc4 Nf6 (4... c5 5. O-O cxd4 6. c3 Nf6 7. e5 dxe5 8. Nxe5 O-O 9. cxd4 Nc6 $15 {Basman-Nunn, [date unknown]}) 5. Nc3 (5. Qe2 c6 6. O-O Nxe4 $2 (6... d5 $11) 7. Bxf7+ Kxf7 8. Qxe4 Rf8 9. Qh4 Kg8 10. Bg5 $14 {Basman-Nunn, [date unknown]}) 5... O-O 6. O-O Nxe4 7. Bxf7+ (7. Nxe4 d5 {leaves White little to play for and is in any case repugnant to Basman's soaring spirit (Golombek, The Times)}) 7... Rxf7 8. Nxe4 h6 9. Be3 Bg4 10. Ned2 Nc6 11. c3 g5 12. Qb3 Na5 13. Qa4 b6 14. b4 Bd7 15. Qd1 Nc6 16. Rc1 g4 17. Ne1 e5 18. d5 Ne7 19. Ne4 Nf5 20. Ng3 Nxe3 21. fxe3 Rxf1+ 22. Nxf1 Qg5 23. Qe2 Rf8 24. c4 h5 25. c5 bxc5 26. bxc5 Bh6 27. cxd6 cxd6 28. Rc7 Qf6 29. Ng3 Bb5 {Sources: Secrets of Grandmaster Chess by John Nunn (Batsford, 1997), p41; The Times, 22 September 1973} 0-1

