1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d3 Nc6 4. g3 d6 5. Bg2 Nf6 6. O-O Be7 7. Nc3 O-O 8. Qe1 Nd7 9. Be3 b6 10. Nd2 Bb7 11. f4 a6 12. f5 Nde5 13. Ne2 Qc7 14. fxe6 fxe6 15. Nf4 Bc8 16. Qe2 Bd7 17. c3 Nd8 18. Nf3 Nef7 19. Qd2 Re8 20. Rf2 Bc6 21. Raf1 Bf8 22. c4 b5 23. Ne1 bxc4 24. dxc4 Qb7 25. Nfd3 Bxe4 26. Bxe4 Qxe4 27. Rf4 Qb7 28. Rg4 e5 29. Qf2 Ne6 30. Ng2 Nd4 31. Nh4 Re6 32. Nf5 Rae8 33. Bxd4 cxd4 {... and now an extraordinary finish...} 34. Nb4 $5 {I was completely baffled by this and suspected a score error until turning on Stockfish 17 - which told me it was White's best move!} Rg6 $2 (34... Qxb4 $4 35. Nxg7 $3 {was the move I missed, but Basman didn't fall for it. However, he did fall for something which his opponent didn't see.}) (34... h5 $19) 35. Rxg6 $2 (35. Nd5 $3 {equalises. If} Rxg4 36. Qf3 $1 {threatening the rook and also a major cheapo with Nf6+ and Qxb7.}) 35... hxg6 36. Nh4 Ng5 {Source: Basman scoresheet (https://michael-basman-legacy.github.io/scoresheets/1973/Hammersmith%2012-4-73.pdf)} 0-1

