1. f4 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 g6 4. c3 Bg7 5. d3 O-O 6. Nh3 c5 7. O-O Nc6 8. Na3 b6 ({Basman had won two games with this line after Black played} 8... e5 {e.g. Basman,M (2385)-Whiteley,A (2340)/BCF-ch Eastbourne 1973 (6)/ 1-0}) 9. Nf2 Bb7 10. e4 dxe4 11. dxe4 Qxd1 12. Rxd1 {This is almost the same position (with colours reversed) as Fraguela v Keene, Torremolinos 1976 (CHESS, June 1976, Vol.41/747-8, pp297-298).} Rfd8 13. Re1 Na5 14. e5 Ne8 15. g4 Bxg2 16. Kxg2 Nc7 {Keene reckons this position is better for White, although I'm not sure why. Basman's plan is certainly incorrect though.} 17. f5 Nd5 18. c4 $2 (18. Bg5 Nc6 19. e6 gxf5 20. gxf5 Rf8 21. Rad1 fxe6 22. fxe6 Rad8 $15) 18... Nb4 19. Bg5 Nac6 20. f6 exf6 21. exf6 h6 22. Bh4 g5 23. fxg7 gxh4 24. Re2 Rd4 25. Nb5 Rxc4 26. Nd6 Rc2 27. Rae1 Rxe2 28. Rxe2 Kxg7 29. Nf5+ Kf8 30. a3 Nd5 31. Rd2 Rd8 32. Ne4 Nf4+ 33. Kf3 Rxd2 34. Nxd2 Nd3 35. Nxh6 Nxb2 36. Ke4 c4 37. Nb1 {We were both short of time in the last few moves up to the time control} Ke7 $2 (37... Nd1 $142) 38. Nf5+ Kf6 $2 39. h3 Nd1 40. Nxh4 Nf2+ $6 41. Kd5 Na5 42. Nf3 $2 Nxh3 43. Nc3 Nf2 $2 (43... Nf4+ 44. Kd4 Ne6+ 45. Kd5 Ke7 46. Ne5 Nc7+ 47. Kd4 Ke6 48. Nxc4 Nxc4 49. Kxc4 Ke5 50. Ne2 a6 51. Nd4 f6 52. Nf5 Nb5 53. Kb4 Nd4 54. Ne3 Nc6+ 55. Kc3 b5 56. Kd3 Nb8 57. Ng2 Nd7 58. Kc3 Ke4 {should still win.}) 44. Ne5 Nd3 45. Nxc4 Nxc4 46. Kxc4 Ne5+ 47. Kb5 Nxg4 48. Ka6 Ne5 49. Kxa7 {Sources: Roger Emerson; https://michael-basman-legacy.github.io/scoresheets/1976/Charlton%2018-6-76.pdf (with some scoring errors - stops scoring at move 39)} 1/2-1/2

