{Judging from the notation (descriptive) and the handwriting, this is Macdonald-Ross's scoresheet. Unfortunately he was as prone to scoring errors as Basman himself!} 1. d4 c6 2. e4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. c4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Be6 6. c5 Nc6 7. Bf4 {('B-B4')} g6 {('P-N3')} 8. Bb5 Bg7 9. Be5 O-O 10. Bxc6 {('BxN')} bxc6 11. Nge2 Bh6 12. Bf4 Bg7 13. Be5 Rb8 14. b3 ({Hard to understand why White would not have taken the exchange with} 14. Bxb8 {but the score as interpreted here seems to make sense otherwise. JS}) 14... Rb7 15. O-O Bf5 16. Ng3 Qd7 17. Qe2 Be6 18. f4 Bf5 19. Qa6 Rb4 20. Rad1 Ne8 21. Nxf5 gxf5 {('PxB')} 22. Bxg7 Kxg7 23. Qe2 Nf6 24. Qe5 Rg8 25. Ne2 a5 26. Ng3 Kg6 27. Rd3 Ng4 28. Qe1 h6 29. a4 {... hereafter moves recorded as dashes up to move 38 when the game presumably ended, followed by a not very successful attempt to record a few moves after the event... 29...R-N4 30 Q-B3 NB3 31 Q-B(?)2 Q? 32 QQ1... 35 R-R3... Source: Macdonald-Ross scoresheet (https://michael-basman-legacy.github.io/scoresheets/1976/London%20Open%2030-7-76.pdf)} 0-1

