1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 Nf6 3. f4 c6 4. b3 Bf5 5. Bb2 e6 6. e3 Be7 7. Nf3 O-O 8. O-O a5 9. a4 Na6 10. h3 h6 11. Kh2 Nb4 12. d3 Bh7 13. Ne5 Nd7 14. Ng4 Qb6 15. Qe2 Qa6 16. Rd1 Rae8 17. Na3 Bd6 18. e4 f5 19. e5 Be7 20. Nf2 Qb6 21. d4 Kh8 22. Bc1 Rg8 23. c3 Na6 24. Rb1 g5 25. Nc2 Rg7 26. Nd3 Reg8 27. Bh1 Nf8 28. Rg1 Qd8 29. Be3 g4 30. Bf2 h5 31. h4 Ng6 32. Qe1 b6 33. b4 axb4 {(first capture of the game)} 34. Ncxb4 {('Nxb4' - first ambiguous move of the game!)} Nb8 35. Rb2 Qc7 36. Qb1 Nd7 37. Rc2 c5 38. dxc5 bxc5 39. Na6 Qd8 40. Naxc5 {('Nxc5')} Nxc5 41. Nxc5 Bxc5 42. Bxc5 Nxf4 43. gxf4 Qxh4+ 44. Kg2 Bg6 45. Bd4 Be8 46. a5 Ba4 47. Rb2 Qh3+ {... hereafter the scoring becomes incomprehensible. What probably happened was:} 48. Kf2 g3+ 49. Ke1 g2 50. Bxg2 Rxg2 51. Rbxg2 Rxg2 52. Rxg2 Qxg2 {and a draw was agreed after about 60 moves. Source: Basman scoresheet (https://michael-basman-legacy.github.io/scoresheets/1976/London%20Open%2030-7-76.pdf)} 1/2-1/2

