{White essays 5 Be3 but Black's answer gains him the advantage. A dashing sacrifice, however, puts White back in the game and Black in the soup. This was the debut of the system as we know it.} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 a6 3. Nf3 b5 4. Bd3 Bb7 5. Be3 Nf6 6. Nbd2 c5 $1 7. dxc5 Ng4 8. Bg5 f6 9. Bh4 Bxc5 10. h3 Nh6 11. e5 g5 12. Ne4 Bxe4 13. Bxe4 Ra7 14. Bg3 f5 15. Bd3 Nc6 16. Qe2 Nf7 17. O-O Kf8 18. a4 b4 19. c3 bxc3 20. bxc3 h5 21. Rad1 Qb6 22. h4 f4 ({For equality Black may play} 22... g4 23. Nd4 Nxd4 24. cxd4 Bxd4 25. Bxa6 {. He plays for more.}) 23. Bh2 g4 24. Bxf4 $1 {A bold sacrifice.} gxf3 25. Qxf3 Rg8 26. Qxh5 Ne7 27. Be4 Qc7 28. Rd3 Rh8 29. Bh7 $1 Nf5 30. Rf3 Qc6 31. Bh6+ Ke8 32. Bg7 Qxf3 33. Qxf3 Rxh7 34. Bf6 Be7 35. Rb1 Bxf6 36. exf6 N7h6 37. Qh5+ Kd8 38. g4 d6 39. gxf5 exf5 {Source: St George's Defence by MJ Basman (Audio Chess)} 1-0

