1. d4 e6 2. e4 a6 3. Nf3 b5 4. Bd3 Bb7 5. Be3 Nf6 6. Nbd2 Ng4 ({Better is} 6... c5 {as in Lexton-Basman.}) 7. Bf4 c5 8. c3 Nc6 9. e5 ({Premature: simply} 9. O-O {leaves Black out on a limb; probably his best move then is} Nf6) (9. d5 exd5 10. exd5 Ne7 11. c4 Ng6 12. Bg3 Qe7+ {is unclear.}) 9... cxd4 10. cxd4 Nb4 11. Be4 Nd5 ({Simpler is} 11... Bxe4 12. Nxe4 Nd5 $11) 12. O-O {Taking advantage of the pin.} h5 13. h3 Nh6 14. Bg5 Qb6 15. Nh4 {White decides to chance the complications.} Qxd4 16. Qxh5 {Here White offered a draw. Black, disarmed, declined and played} Qxe5 $2 17. Ng6 $1 {Now Black cannot avoid the loss of a piece.} Nf6 18. Nxe5 Nxh5 19. Bxb7 Ra7 20. Rac1 Nf6 21. Rc8+ Ke7 22. Bf3 Nf5 23. Ne4 Nd4 24. Rd1 d6 25. Rxd4 dxe5 26. Rdd8 Rc7 27. Re8+ Kd7 28. Nxf6+ {Source: St George's Defence by MJ Basman (Audio Chess)} 1-0

