1. e4 g5 2. d4 h6 3. h4 gxh4 4. Rxh4 d5 5. exd5 e6 6. Rh5 Nf6 (6... exd5 {Basman}) 7. dxe6 Bxe6 8. Nc3 Nxh5 9. Qxh5 Bb4 10. Nge2 Nc6 11. Be3 Qd7 12. a3 Bg4 13. Qb5 a6 14. Qd3 Bxc3+ 15. Qxc3 O-O-O 16. f3 Be6 17. O-O-O Ne7 18. Nf4 Nd5 19. Nxd5 Bxd5 20. Qd2 Qc6 21. Kb1 h5 22. Bg5 Rde8 23. Bf4 $2 (23. Bh4 {Basman}) 23... Bc4 24. Be5 Rhg8 25. d5 Bxd5 26. Qd4 Bb3 $4 {"This move is fatally flawed, but White, his confidence ebbing fast due to the unexpected resistance he has been facing, does not spot the error." (Basman)} 27. Bd3 $4 ({"White assumes that} 27. cxb3 {will fail to} Rd8 {. However, he misses} 28. Rc1 $1 Rxd4 29. Rxc6 Rd1+ 30. Rc1 {which leaves him with two bishops against a rook." (Basman)}) 27... Rd8 28. Qe3 (28. Qa7 $2 Rxd3 $3 29. Qa8+ Kd7 30. Rxd3+ Ke6 $19) 28... Bc4 29. Qa7 Bxd3 30. cxd3 Qb6 31. Qxb6 cxb6 {"Played with care, this position should be a win for Black. The game later went to an adjourn­ment but Speelman did not put up a stern defence in the second session." (Basman)} 32. g3 Kd7 33. Bf4 Kc6 34. Rc1+ Kb5 35. Rc7 Rxd3 36. Rxf7 Rxf3 37. Rf5+ Kc4 38. Rxh5 Kb3 39. Rh1 Rf2 40. Bc1 Rxg3 41. Rh7 b5 $1 42. Rc7 (42. Rxb7 Rg1 $19) 42... b6 43. Rc6 Rh3 44. Rg6 Rc2 45. Rg1 a5 46. Rg6 Rc5 {Sources: bulletin; 'The Killer Grob' by Michael Basman (Pergamon, 1988)} 0-1

