{Day two began with me arriving 20 minutes late for the first game which in a half hour time limit is a large deficit.} 1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Qe2 Be7 4. d4 Bh4+ 5. Kd1 Ne7 6. Bxf4 d5 7. e5 Ng6 8. Be3 O-O 9. Nf3 f6 10. g3 Bg4 11. e6 Re8 12. gxh4 Nxh4 13. Nbd2 Rxe6 14. Qf2 Nf5 15. Bf4 {"after which White had won a piece but still remained under pressure. With time trouble a permanent fixture of my position, I was relieved when Black overlooked a check and allowed QxK! (you can do this in quick chess.) Source: CHESS, February 1982, Vol.46/871-2, p344} 1-0

