1. g4 d5 2. h3 e5 3. Bg2 Ne7 4. c4 dxc4 5. Na3 Ng6 6. Nxc4 Be7 7. d3 Nd7 8. Nf3 c6 {[ This gives me my chance ]} 9. h4 $1 Nxh4 10. Nxh4 Bxh4 11. Nd6+ Kf8 12. Qb3 {[ Sheâ??s lucky sheâ??s not just losing a piece ]} Qf6 ({After} 12... Qe7 {I just play} 13. Nxc8 (13. Rxh4 Nc5 {is not so clear.}) 13... Rxc8 14. Qxb7 {smashing her.}) 13. Ne4 Qe7 14. g5 f5 {She is just able to save the piece with this.} 15. Rxh4 fxe4 16. Be3 exd3 17. Qxd3 Nb6 18. Qc2 {[ ?c5 is not just a cheapo, but the start of a great strategical plan! ]} Kg8 19. Bc5 Qf7 20. Be4 g6 21. O-O-O Be6 ({Maybe she should have tried} 21... Bf5) ({RR} 21... Qxa2 22. Bxg6) 22. Rd6 Nc4 23. Rd3 {[ But this is really unfortunate, because now I come at her from the other direction! ]} Kg7 24. Rf3 Qd7 25. b3 Nb6 26. Qc3 {[ Now we start an attack on the dark squares.]} Qc7 27. Rf6 Rae8 28. Rh6 {[ So now 29 ?fxg6+ is the threat ]} Nd5 29. Bxd5 Bxd5 30. Bd6 {? [ And she resigned. Note how every White piece is on a dark square!.]} 1-0

